// World time: how fast the world ages, independent of how fast it falls.
//
// Generated by the tunables panel (`O` -> WORLD, `S` to save), so this file
// is rewritten wholesale on save and carries no comments the panel would
// destroy -- these ones live above the struct and survive because the
// serializer only ever replaces the parenthesised body below. Every field's
// real reasoning is on `sim::clock::Clock`.
//
// Each knob is "N times slower than baseline", and 1 is the behaviour the
// engine had before any of this existed.
//
// **This file is read by the app and by nothing else.** `World::new` leaves
// the clock at baseline, so every test, harness and acceptance scene is
// untouched by what is set here. That divergence is deliberate: it is what
// lets the app ship a playable day length without re-baselining several
// hundred guards. Harnesses take the knobs as explicit arguments instead.
(
    day_minutes: 8,
    weather_slowdown: 1,
    growth_slowdown: 1,
    creature_slowdown: 1,
    gnome_slowdown: 1,
)
